 32-bit architectures
Message-ID: <CAM8zJQvwPLL4CA8itGP=5t1aTnxb7k5uFRY=gYhXihbhSaq7ag@mail.gmail.com>

Source: r-cran-wgcna
Version: 1.72-5-1
Severity: serious
Tags: ftbfs
Control: affects -1 + src:r-bioc-netsam

Hi Maintainer

As can be seen in experimental [1], r-cran-wcgna is missing a
build-dependency on 32-bit architectures.

Dependency installability problem for r-cran-wgcna on armhf:

r-cran-wgcna build-depends on:
- r-bioc-annotationdbi:armhf (>= 1.66.0)
r-bioc-annotationdbi depends on missing:
- r-bioc-iranges:armhf (>= 2.38.1)

Although r-cran-wgcna 1.72-5-1 successfully built in unstable while
this dependency was still available, it is unable to migrate to
testing [2] and blocks the migration of r-bioc-netsam [3] as well.

I think removing r-cran-wgcna's 32-bit binary packages should be
sufficient to resolve this.

Regards
Graham


[1] https://buildd.debian.org/status/package.php?p=r-cran-wgcna&suite=experimental
[2] https://tracker.debian.org/pkg/r-cran-wgcna
[3] https://tracker.debian.org/pkg/r-bioc-netsam


